# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MediKiosk configuration
#
# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL. The app runs with no .env file at all.
# To use it: copy this file to  .env  and fill in what you want.
#
# Never commit .env, and never paste a real key into a chat window.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. AI  (clinical summaries + reading scanned documents) ──────────
# Without this the app still runs: summaries become a plain assembly of the
# patient's own answers, and scanned documents are stored as images without
# being read. Everything else works unchanged.
#
# Get a key: console.anthropic.com → API keys → Create key.
# A few dollars of credit covers a hackathon comfortably.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5


# ── 2. SMS  (OTP codes and ABHA delivery) ────────────────────────────
# console  → codes print in this terminal and show on screen. Free. Default.
# msg91    → India. Cheapest. Needs a DLT-registered template (takes days).
# fast2sms → India. Simpler signup. DLT still applies for transactional SMS.
# twilio   → Easiest signup, works immediately, worst Indian rates.
#
SMS_PROVIDER=console

# MSG91 — control.msg91.com
# MSG91_AUTH_KEY=
# MSG91_SENDER_ID=MEDKSK
# MSG91_TEMPLATE_ID=

# Fast2SMS — fast2sms.com/dashboard/dev-api
# FAST2SMS_API_KEY=

# Twilio — console.twilio.com
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_FROM=+1...


# ── 3. Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PORT=3000
# HOSPITAL_NAME=All India Institute of Ayurveda

# ── 4. Firebase (optional backend storage & files) ───────────────────
# FIREBASE_DB_URL=https://<your-project-id>.firebaseio.com
# FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=<your-project-id>.appspot.com
#
# Remember to generate a new private key from Firebase Console -> Project Settings -> Service Accounts
# and save it in the project root as `firebase-service-account.json`.
